  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of stereoisomers that can exist for M is<br />\r\n\r\n<br />\r\n\r\n<br />\r\n\r\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image21-60853377-f00a-4861-b7df-38dacb7ba8d4.jpg\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Total number of stereoisomers = 2. Although it has two chiral carbon so&nbsp;it is expected to have&nbsp;four stereoisomer, but this molecular cannot show geometrical isomerism so only mirror image will be other stereoisomer. Hence the possible number of stereoisomer will be 2 only.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image22-c59c44c9-fd0b-44ae-ba41-4e831aa0ded7.png\" /><br />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
